# Common Rules

## Naming

| Type | File | Notes |
|------|------|-------|
| Nest controller | `auth.controller.ts` | Nest style under `apps/api` |
| Nest service | `auth.service.ts` | injectable class |
| Nest module | `auth.module.ts` | |
| Web feature / page | `sign-in-form.tsx`, `page.tsx` | kebab-case files; PascalCase components |
| shadcn UI | under `apps/web/components/ui/` | |

- Classes/interfaces: `PascalCase`
- Functions/vars: `camelCase`
- Constants: `as const` objects, not TypeScript `enum`

## Style

- 2 spaces, single quotes, ~100 cols, no semicolons, no trailing commas
- Prefer `import type`; avoid `any`; prefer `| null` over `undefined` for optionals

## Constants

Put shared constants in one summary file per package (`apps/web/constants/index.ts`, `apps/api` equivalent, or `@elynd/shared`). Split only past ~500 lines. Status/type/mode/API literals used ≥2 times must be constants—no scattered magic strings.

## Services vs utils

- **Services**: Nest injectable classes / application services with ports
- **Utils**: plain functions/values under `utils/` or `lib/`, never mixed into service folders as catch-alls

## Quality

Project verification commands (run the smallest relevant set before claiming done):

```bash
pnpm run lint
pnpm run typecheck
pnpm run test
```
